# Data artifacts — published to R2, never committed
# The payloads are R2-published and never committed - but manifest.yaml IS the record of what we fetch,
# its checksum and its licence, and three tests read it. Ignoring the whole directory made it invisible to
# git while every local run stayed green, and CI failed 3 tests with no name attached. Ignore the payloads.
services/etl/inputs/*
!services/etl/inputs/manifest.yaml
services/etl/work/
services/routing/graph-cache/
*.osm.pbf
*.pmtiles
corpus*.sqlite

# Secrets — never in the repo, see CLAUDE.md
.env
.env.*
*.p8
*.p12
.netrc
